## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical streaming state management, windowing, and late data handling in KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Windowed aggregation by userId using 10-minute tumbling windows
- Watermark and 2-minute lateness tolerance for out-of-order events
- Per-window state management with eviction policies
- At-least-once guarantees via offset committing after emission
- Canary coverage with mixed event timings

## Code Example
```javascript
const WINDOW_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000;
const LATE_MS = 2 * 60 * 1000;

function onMessage(msg, commitFn) {
  const { userId, ts, score } = JSON.parse(msg.value);
  const windowStart = Math.floor(ts / WINDOW_MS) * WINDOW_MS;
  const windowEnd = windowStart + WINDOW_MS;
  const stateKey = `${userId}:${windowStart}`;

  if (ts < watermark - LATE_MS) return; // drop late

  state[stateKey] = (state[stateKey] || 0) + score;
  watermark = Math.max(watermark, ts);

  if (watermark >= windowEnd + LATE_MS && !emitted.has(stateKey)) {
    emit('activity_agg', { userId, windowStart, windowEnd, sum: state[stateKey] });
    emitted.add(stateKey);
    delete state[stateKey];
  }

  commitFn();
}

function onPartitionsAssigned(partitions) {
  state = restoreState(partitions);
  watermark = restoreWatermark();
}

function onPartitionsRevoked() {
  checkpointState(state, watermark);
  state = {};
}

function commitOffsets(offsets) {
  consumer.commit(offsets);
}
```

